      "side": 1,
      "message": "Based on your suggestion, I updated the patch to handle this in NetworkStatsRecorder.loadLocked() instead of trying to make assumptions about NetworkStatsHistory callers.\n\n1)NetworkStatsHistory.recordData() remains strict and now throws a specific NetworkStatsHistory.NegativeDataException extends IllegalArgumentException when negative values are encountered.\n\n2)NetworkStatsRecorder.loadLocked() now catches NegativeDataException explicitly and routes it to the existing recovery path (Log.wtf(...) + recoverAndDeleteData()), matching the behavior we already have for IOException/OutOfMemoryError.\n\n3)Added a unit test in NetworkStatsRecorderTest to verify wipe-on-error behavior for NegativeDataException.",
